WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.540
The O R W base and Meta design documents have different scopes.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.300
The base defines shared frame and power interfaces, while leaving external dimensions

3
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.280
and maximum payload to the implementation.

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.900
The Meta document describes a particular rack-frame implementation.

5
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:18.240
Its nominal dimensions are two thousand three hundred ninety millimeters high, twelve

6
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.480
hundred millimeters wide, and twelve hundred nineteen millimeters deep.

7
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.000
These are implementation dimensions, not a universal O R W envelope.

8
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.220
The controlling drawings and tolerances remain necessary for an engineering comparison.

9
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.340
Keep revisions together.

10
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.800
A Summit presentation can show a development configuration or a differently stated

11
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:37.540
nominal value.

12
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.960
Don't combine that value with the published drawing to create a new

13
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.060
geometry that neither source specifies.

14
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.880
For a supplier proposal, identify the actual drawing revision and configured accessories,

15
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.380
then compare its complete envelope to the site.

16
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.200
The course plate helps locate the relevant interfaces; it is not a

17
00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.040
substitute for the source drawing or an installation survey.

